course: dictionary
lesson: 8156
title: Research as a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Research can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, research means careful study to find out new facts: «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.»
explain: As a verb, to research means to look for information about a topic, for example in books or online. A pupil might research animals or countries for a school project.
explain: Notice that the noun research is uncountable, so we say do research or some research, not a research. The clues in «Research on games is mixed» tell you it means the study of something, not one single thing.
fact: Research means careful study to find out new facts or information.
fact: To research means to look for information about a topic, for example in books or online.
fact: Research is uncountable as a noun, so say do research, not a research.
fact: Common phrases: do research, research into, research project, carry out research.
fact: Good researchers use trusted sites and check their facts before they write anything down.
exercise: «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» What does research mean here? | A kind of sunlight | A playground game | *Careful study to find out new facts | Reading a comic
exercise: Maya wants to research volcanoes for her project. What does research mean in this sentence? | *Look for information about the topic, in books or online | Throw stones into a lake | Eat her lunch quickly | Draw a picture of a volcano
exercise: Which phrase is correct? | researchings | a research | *do research | three researches
test: According to the text, what can too much gaming push out? | Maths tests | *Sleep, exercise and homework | Pet dogs | Music and painting
test: Riya says only scientists in labs can do research. Is she right? | Yes, only scientists in labs | Yes, but only on Tuesdays | No, only zoos do research | *No, anyone can research a topic, for example in books or online
exam: Which sentence uses research as a verb? | Do some research before you start | *Ben will research the rainforest for his project | The research was very careful | Research suggests sleep helps learning
